original_row.English:
There are those who receive inheritance and transmit inheritance;
and there are those who receive inheritance but do not transmit inheritance;
transmit inheritance but do not receive inheritance;
neither receive inheritance nor transmit inheritance.
The following receive inheritance and transmit inheritance:
a father vis-à-vis his sons;
sons vis-à-vis their father;
brothers of the same father [vis-à-vis each other]—
these receive inheritance and transmit inheritance.
A man from his mother;
a man from his wife;
and the sons of sisters—
these receive inheritance but do not transmit inheritance.
A woman to her sons;
and a woman to her husband;
and a mother’s brothers—
these transmit inheritance but do not receive inheritance. And maternal brothers—
these neither receive inheritance nor transmit inheritance.

